      },
      "lineNbr": 399,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-18T16:47:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here you document the fields `uor` and `pdr` as temporary.  But you do need to track the current data role and power role. The SET_UOR command has this text:\n\n\"It is illegal for the OPM to set/clear Bit0 and Bit1 at the same time.\nThis command is valid only if connector supports PD\"\n\nFor SET_PDR, you can se just bit 2 (accept power swap), but I recommend we always set our current power role when sending SET_PDR to match the SET_UOR implementation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 399,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 399,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "9a2736855185e226d17a34d04fecc1955e623195",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d055017b_e127c3b3",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1448,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-18T16:47:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is invalid. This clears both the DFP and UFP mode bits.  We need to retain the current data role and set the correct bit.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1448,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1448,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "9a2736855185e226d17a34d04fecc1955e623195",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3f2d48b_01957b39",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1468,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-18T16:47:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This clears SNK and SRC bits - while this is allowed, we probably should set the bit corresponding to our current power role.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1468,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1468,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "9a2736855185e226d17a34d04fecc1955e623195",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8efe6e72_09e13fea",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-17T17:57:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You also need to set `accept_dr_swap`, otherwise the PDC will reject swaps.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1499,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "9a2736855185e226d17a34d04fecc1955e623195",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9aecfeb2_2cda1db9",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-17T18:07:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "accept_dr_swap is set to 1 by default, but can be updated with the pdc_power_mgmt_accept_data_swap API.\n\nIMO accept_dr_swap shouldn\u0027t be part of this register.",
      "parentUuid": "8efe6e72_09e13fea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1499,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "9a2736855185e226d17a34d04fecc1955e623195",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b29375f_ba405575",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-17T19:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The documentation of the `uor` field indicates that it\u0027s a temporary variable.  I would expect all sub-fields to be set each time you send SET_UOR.\n\nAlso pdc_power_mgmt_accept_power_swap() explicitly clears both the swap_to_dfp and swap_to_ufp bits, which is not permitted.",
      "parentUuid": "9aecfeb2_2cda1db9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1499,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "9a2736855185e226d17a34d04fecc1955e623195",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "10491e86_b85c2d9c",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/pd_controller/pdc_power_mgmt.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 1499,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-18T14:00:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I couldn\u0027t find in the UCSI 3.0 spec where it states that the bit2 in the UOR register is temporary.\n\nFrom table 6-20: SET_UOR command\n```\nIf bit 0 is set, then the connector\nshall initiate swap to DFP if not\nalready operating in DFP mode.\n\nIf bit 1 is set, then the connector\nshall initiate swap to UFP if not\nalready operating in UFP mode.\n\nIf bit 2 is set, then the connector\nshall accept role swap change\nrequests from the port partner.\nIf this bit is cleared, then connector\nshall reject Role Swap change\nrequests from the port partner.\n```\nSo I keep a copy of bit2 in accept_dr_swap, so it\u0027s not clobbered when requesting a data role swap.\n\nI removed the code that sets bit0 and bit1.",
      "parentUuid": "5b29375f_ba405575",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1499,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1499,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "9a2736855185e226d17a34d04fecc1955e623195",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
